hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1510","I am Abu Al-Khattab Ziyad bin Yahya, and Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala Al-Sana’ani. They said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us. H Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abdul Wahhab told us, they said: Khaled told us. H, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Ulayya narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwayrith, and this Hadith of Bundar, who said: I and a friend of mine came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when we wanted to close, he said to us: “When the time for prayer comes, give us the call to prayer, then “Establish them, then let the eldest of you lead you in prayer.” Al-Dawraqi added in his hadith: He said: So I said to Abu Qilaba: Where is the recitation? He said: They were close"
